            <ArticleTitle>Do autologous blood and PRP injections effectively treat tennis elbow?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>635</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Both approaches reduce pain, but the improvement with platelet-rich plasma (PRP) is not clinically meaningful. Autologous blood injections (ABIs) are more effective than corticosteroid injections for reducing pain and disability in patients with tennis elbow in both the short and long term.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
